 "result": "All of this is in `src/tessel/views.py`.\n\n**Classes**\n- `View` (line 16) is the base class.\n- `VerbView(View)` (line 138) is the one that dispatches by HTTP method.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Collecting methods.** `VerbView.__init_subclass__` (line 165) runs when your subclass is defined. If the class doesn't set `methods` itself, it gathers the uppercase names of the HTTP-verb methods the class defines, such as `get` and `post`, plus any `methods` inherited from base classes. It stores them in `cls.methods`.\n2. **Building the view function.** `View.to_view_func(name, ...)` (line 86) is a classmethod that returns a plain `view(**kwargs)` function.\n   - It creates the instance per request, or once if `init_every_request` is `False`.\n   - It calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` through `active_app.ensure_sync`.\n   - It applies any `cls.decorators`.\n   - It attaches `view_class`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` to the function. Route registration uses `methods` to decide which HTTP methods the route accepts.\n3. **Per-request dispatch.** `VerbView.run_view` (line 182) does `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`.\n   - A `HEAD` request falls back to `get` when there is no `head` handler.\n   - It calls the handler with the URL kwargs.",
